qa:AG18-QA-002
    a qa:Finding ;
    qa:findingId "AG18-QA-002" ;
    qa:phase "phase-AG" ;
    qa:title "SendResponseEnvelope::{Sent,Acknowledged} never deleted/deprecated" ;
    qa:severity "blocking" ;
    qa:pattern "rename-not-remove" ;
    qa:repeatable true ;
    qa:sourceReviewers "req-qa (ATM-QA-002)", "arch-qa (ARCH-001)", "ruthless-boundary-qa (RBQA-F002)" ;
    qa:description """crates/atm-core/src/protocol.rs:42-45 defines `pub enum SendResponseEnvelope { Sent(SendOutcome), Acknowledged(AckOutcome) }` with no #[deprecated] attribute. docs/plans/phase-AG/sprint-AG18.md explicitly names this type for deletion in AG.18 (lines ~121, ~148, ~158), or, if removal must be staged, for deprecation in AG.18 with deletion no later than the immediate follow-on sprint that collapses the last caller. Neither happened: the enum remains fully defined and undeprecated through AG.18, AG.19, AG.20, and the in-progress AG.21, and is actively constructed/matched at 15+ call sites per worktree, including crates/atm/src/composition.rs, crates/atm-graft/src/lib.rs, crates/atm-daemon-client/src/rpc.rs, crates/atm-core/src/protocol.rs (definition site), crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs, crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs (AG.21 only), crates/atm-daemon/src/non_claude_outbound_runtime.rs, crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/dispatch_delivery.rs, and multiple test modules (tests_post_send_graft_warning.rs, tests/runtime_root/*.rs, peer_transport/tests/harness.rs).""" ;
    qa:sweepScope "repeatable-pattern sweep across all worktrees with real commits (AG.18-AG.21) for any remaining SendResponseEnvelope::Sent/Acknowledged construction or match sites" .

